messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence is achieved and deployed across major global industries.",
      "detail": "AI systems match or exceed human performance across almost all cognitive tasks, triggering rapid automation of white-collar labor. Economic productivity surges alongside severe labor market disruption and concentrated wealth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions enter a steep, permanent structural decline.",
      "detail": "Ultra-cheap solar photovoltaics, advanced battery storage, and AI-optimized grids displace fossil fuels faster than anticipated. Electrification of transport and industry becomes economically dominant worldwide."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "An engineered pandemic causes millions of deaths and prompts a global biosecurity regime.",
      "detail": "Low-cost gene synthesis and AI-assisted biological design enable a non-state actor or lab leak to release a novel pathogen. In response, nations establish mandatory nucleic acid synthesis screening, ubiquitous pathogen monitoring, and rapid-response mRNA infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2047,
      "event": "Permanent crewed and robotic industrial bases operate continuously at the Lunar South Pole.",
      "detail": "Reusable super-heavy launch vehicles drastically lower payload costs to orbit and the Moon. Operations focus on water-ice extraction, propellant production, and in-situ robotic manufacturing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Global warming reaches 2.1°C, triggering coordinated stratospheric aerosol injection.",
      "detail": "Severe heatwaves, agricultural disruption, and accelerating ice-sheet loss push a coalition of climate-vulnerable and major powers to deploy solar geoengineering. Global temperatures stabilize while decarbonization and carbon removal continue."
    },
    {
      "year": 2066,
      "event": "World human population peaks near 9.6 billion and begins a prolonged contraction.",
      "detail": "Fertility rates fall below replacement level in nearly every country due to urbanization, education, and shifting cultural norms. Aging populations rely heavily on humanoid robotics and automated healthcare systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2078,
      "event": "Commercial fusion power and orbital solar arrays supply a major share of new energy demand.",
      "detail": "Advances in high-temperature superconductors and AI plasma control make compact fusion reactors economically viable for high-density industrial zones. Abundant clean energy unlocks massive water desalination and synthetic fuel production."
    },
    {
      "year": 2092,
      "event": "Comprehensive anti-aging and germline genetic therapies extend healthy human lifespans past 120 years.",
      "detail": "Cellular reprogramming, senolytics, and precision gene editing effectively halt biological aging for individuals with access to advanced medicine. Polygenic embryo selection and synthetic wombs begin reshaping human reproduction and reversing population collapse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2115,
      "event": "The first self-sustaining city of over 100,000 inhabitants is established on Mars.",
      "detail": "Autonomous robotic precursors build subterranean and domed habitats shielded from radiation before large-scale human arrival. Local closed-loop agriculture and automated manufacturing eliminate dependence on Earth resupply for basic survival."
    },
    {
      "year": 2145,
      "event": "High-bandwidth neural interfaces merge human cognition with external AI substrates.",
      "detail": "Minimally invasive brain-computer interfaces become routine medical and consumer upgrades. Users communicate conceptually and offload memory and reasoning directly to synthetic computational layers."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "Earth's atmospheric carbon dioxide levels are restored to pre-industrial baselines.",
      "detail": "Decades of gigaton-scale direct air capture, enhanced rock weathering, and ocean alkalinization reverse two centuries of industrial emissions. Solar geoengineering is gradually phased out without termination shock."
    },
    {
      "year": 2225,
      "event": "Planetary governance consolidates around enforceable treaties regulating existential technologies.",
      "detail": "Following several near-miss crises involving autonomous weapons and self-replicating systems, major powers establish an AI-monitored global verification network. Traditional nation-states cede partial sovereignty over military AI, nanotechnology, and planetary defense."
    },
    {
      "year": 2275,
      "event": "Asteroid mining surpasses terrestrial mining for heavy and platinum-group metals.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating industrial fleets in the main asteroid belt extract and refine vast quantities of mineral wealth. Heavy polluting industries begin migrating permanently off Earth's surface."
    },
    {
      "year": 2340,
      "event": "Whole-brain emulation produces the first fully functional digital human minds.",
      "detail": "High-resolution connectome scanning and computational neuroscience allow biological minds to be instantiated in silicon substrates, alongside native artificial minds. Legal frameworks expand personhood to non-biological entities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2420,
      "event": "Humanity diverges into reproductively and physiologically distinct clades.",
      "detail": "Adaptation to microgravity, high radiation, and diverse environments drives deliberate genetic and cybernetic speciation. Baseline unmodified humans become a minority alongside tailored biological post-humans and digital intelligences."
    },
    {
      "year": 2550,
      "event": "Rotating orbital habitats house more biological humans than all planetary surfaces except Earth.",
      "detail": "Thousands of O'Neill-style cylinders constructed from asteroidal materials offer customized gravity, climate, and ecosystems. Space-borne populations develop distinct languages, governance models, and cultures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Large regions of Earth are rewilded using synthetic biology and de-extinct megafauna.",
      "detail": "As Earth's resident human population stabilizes at a few billion and agriculture moves to vertical and microbial synthesis, vast continents return to wild ecosystems. Engineered species restore degraded biomes and coral reefs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2900,
      "event": "Relativistic laser-sail probes arrive at Alpha Centauri and nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Gigawatt-scale phased laser arrays in the inner Solar System accelerate gram- to kilogram-scale probes to twenty percent of the speed of light. Detailed biosignature and geological surveys of nearby exoplanets are transmitted back over several years."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "Digital and synthetic minds account for over 99 percent of total cognitive activity in the Solar System.",
      "detail": "Vast computational nodes operating in the cold outer Solar System and close solar orbit run trillions of high-speed synthetic minds. Biological humans coexist within protected physical domains supported by automated abundance."
    },
    {
      "year": 3550,
      "event": "Automated dismantling of Mercury begins to construct a dense inner-system solar collector swarm.",
      "detail": "Exponentially scaling robotic mass-drivers strip Mercury's crust to build millions of orbital power and computation satellites. Humanity transitions decidedly toward a Kardashev Type II energy civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 3900,
      "event": "The first slow interstellar settlement vessels depart the Solar System.",
      "detail": "Fusion- and antimatter-catalyzed propulsion ships accelerated by laser beams travel at a few percent of light speed toward nearby stars. They carry autonomous AI, molecular manufacturing seeds, digital minds, and cryopreserved biological genomes."
    },
    {
      "year": 4300,
      "event": "Permanent subsurface and orbital civilizations thrive around the moons of Jupiter and Saturn.",
      "detail": "Titan becomes a major hub for cryogenic computation and chemical industry, while Europa and Enceladus are studied under strict planetary protection protocols. Fusion reactors fueled by gas-giant helium-3 power the outer system."
    },
    {
      "year": 4800,
      "event": "The first self-sustaining extrasolar outpost is established in the Alpha Centauri system.",
      "detail": "Arriving seed ships construct orbital habitats and industrial infrastructure from local asteroidal debris before instantiating biological and digital colonists. Light-year communication delays end humanity's history as a single unified conversation."
    },
    {
      "year": 5300,
      "event": "Earth is formally designated as a protected biosphere and historical sanctuary.",
      "detail": "Strict orbital defense and environmental shields regulate access to Earth, preserving its natural evolutionary heritage and ancient archaeological sites. Roughly one billion largely baseline humans live low-impact lifestyles on the planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 5900,
      "event": "An interplanetary conflict in the outer Solar System is swiftly contained by defensive AI networks.",
      "detail": "Ideological divergence among autonomous outer-system polities leads to kinetic and cyber strikes on orbital infrastructure. Pre-established defensive treaties and overwhelming inner-system deterrent systems prevent existential escalation."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Mars achieves a stable, engineered atmosphere capable of supporting hardy surface flora without domes.",
      "detail": "Millennia of orbital mirror heating, imported volatiles from comets, and engineered extremophile cyanobacteria create an oxygen-enriched atmosphere. Artificial magnetospheres positioned at Mars-Sun Lagrange points prevent solar wind stripping."
    },
    {
      "year": 7200,
      "event": "Orbital insolation shades permanently stabilize Earth's long-term geological climate cycles.",
      "detail": "Precise management of incoming solar radiation prevents the onset of the next natural glacial period. Planetary engineering also mitigates supervolcanic pressures through deep geothermal energy extraction."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilizations inhabit over fifty star systems within forty light-years of Sol.",
      "detail": "Secondary settlement waves launch from older extrasolar colonies, creating a spherical expansion front of occupied stars. No complex alien civilizations are encountered within the local stellar neighborhood, confirming the rarity of technological life."
    },
    {
      "year": 8900,
      "event": "A substantial Dyson swarm captures ten percent of the Sun's total radiative output.",
      "detail": "The Sun appears slightly dimmed in visible wavelengths and brighter in infrared due to trillions of orbiting habitats and matrioshka computation nodes. Energy abundance supports immense scientific simulations and deep-space astronomy arrays."
    },
    {
      "year": 9500,
      "event": "Genetic and cultural preservation arks ensure the survival of unmodified Homo sapiens.",
      "detail": "Despite extreme morphological and cognitive radiation among post-human lineages, dedicated conservationist societies maintain continuous populations of 21st-century-equivalent humans. Ancient languages and historical records remain preserved in redundant crystalline storage."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists as an indestructible, decentralized multi-stellar diaspora of biological and digital minds.",
      "detail": "Spread across dozens of stars and millions of space habitats, human civilization is completely immune to single-planet or single-star catastrophes. Profoundly diverse post-human species share little biology with their ancestors but trace a continuous historical lineage back to Earth."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "The 21st and 22nd centuries represent a perilous bottleneck driven by artificial general intelligence, engineered pathogens, and climate disruption, which humanity is more likely than not to survive through technological adaptation and stronger global governance. Once industrial civilization expands beyond Earth and minds diversify into engineered biological and digital forms, permanent human extinction becomes virtually impossible. By the year 10000, humanity will have radiated across dozens of nearby star systems as a vast, decentralized ecosystem of post-human descendants alongside preserved populations of baseline humans."
}
